# ---- Virtual environments ----
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---- Python bytecode / build artifacts ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# ---- Generated / benchmark data (never commit large XML) ----
data/
*.xml
*.xml.gz
*.parquet

# ---- Test & lint caches ----
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
coverage.xml
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Hypothesis writes here on every run: its failing-example database, a constants cache
# and a copy of the unicode tables. It also writes a .gitignore of its own, so the
# directory would stay invisible until that file was deleted -- which is exactly the
# failure M12 reported: "it is not in git status" was true and "it was never written
# into the repository" was not. Naming it here means the guarantee does not rest on a
# third-party library hiding itself.
.hypothesis/

# ---- Editors / OS ----
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- Agent workspace metadata (not part of the project) ----
.workbuddy-ai/

# ---- Exception: small committed test fixtures ----
!tests/fixtures/**/*.xml
!tests/fixtures/**/*.xml.gz

# ---- Local working notes: development journals, kept out of the repository ----
# The whole directory, not a list of name patterns. It is not tracked at all (see the
# commit that removed it), so enumerating patterns only creates ways to miss: a new kind
# of internal file -- a preflight note, say -- matches none of them and shows up as
# untracked. Committing something from here on purpose needs `git add -f`, and that
# friction is the point.
docs/

# 本机临时工作区（pytest --basetemp / 探针产物）。只在本机，永不提交。
.scratch/

# GUI 探针在仓库根目录创建的状态目录（`tests/_gui_mem.py` 用 `Path.cwd() / "state"`）。
# 只在本机跑测试时产生，不属于项目内容。
state/

# Where the examples write their output (`examples/*/README.md` say to run from the
# repository root). A run of the Wikipedia example leaves a 1.6 GB document's worth of CSV
# and a report in here, and the point of A3 in the examples brief is that data is never
# committed -- so the directory that catches it has to be ignored by name, in one place,
# rather than by each example remembering to say so.
out/
